        {
          "end_ms": null,
          "error": null,
          "field": "description",
          "page_id": "page-595a917c6dfff68cd6beb209",
          "qa_findings": [],
          "review_status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "segment_id": "seg-24625dd1bd6b8b9b1321b9f4",
          "segment_index": 13,
          "source_segment_id": "seg-24625dd1bd6b8b9b1321b9f4",
          "source_text_sha256": "2b6808f0769e2bed378bc72fdde40656c1ae0dfe4d542423a9aa517c10d05747",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On August 25, 2016, a family observed the starry sky with a telescope. At 10:30 PM, they observed with the naked eye the very quick passage of a phenomenon composed of 5 lights of a yellow-orange color trending towards reddish. No particular noise was heard during the observation, which lasted less than 5 seconds. The only testimony collected reported that during its passage, the PAN occluded the stars. Of average strangeness and good consistency (multiple witnesses, but a unique and fairly precise testimony), the case appears to be a probable misidentification with a fragmented meteor (see the investigation report). The description provided by the witness can evoke several explanatory hypotheses:\n\n• Thai lanterns: The shape of the PAN and the fact that they do not move in the direction of the wind eliminate the first hypothesis;\n\n• A group of birds illuminated by streetlights could potentially explain the observation, but the very high speed of the PAN and the fact that they follow each other in a line present inconsistencies with this explanatory hypothesis;\n\n• That of a fragmented meteor, too weak to be detected by the FRIPON network, can instead explain all elements of the observation: shape of the PAN, very quick movement in a line, color, and the fact that the stars were occluded. The case is classified B, probable misidentification with a fragmented meteor.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "e7b1234a4e8acd1943c41443ef0fa873c3a23bbf0c55d2c509c237fe14b3c512"
        }
      ],
